<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ermengarde of Narbonne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1127–1197</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ermengarde was viscountess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narbonne">Narbonne</a> from 1134 to 1192 and one of the most powerful women of 12th-century southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. She allied with the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, took part in the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> in 1148, sat as a judge and presided over a court praised by troubadours. She abdicated in favour of her nephew Pedro de Lara.</p></div>
